From 8515f6244a8e8e839c5a8e227aa536441a1a8397 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:21:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Idle annotation holder: wake on a watched-file
 change, 60 s fallback for display-only scopes

Deployed P1 run3 (t_3fe574bcd5c5dd01, serve pid 2682517, 600.02 s): lease.kanban-annotation 11.55% of a core
(budget 2.4%), annotation.refresh 10.88% over 294 runs with 0 changes, and every scope's holder_refresh ran
247 times (every ~2.4 s) while only ~30 changed anything.

Five whys: the holder spent its CPU on renewals and probes of scopes nothing had touched -> it re-read every
demanded scope every 20 s and probed (copy load + narrow key) every 2 s past the floor -> it had no cheap way to
know that none of a scope's inputs moved -> the only "moved?" test was the narrow key / exact fingerprint, both
of which open and query the SQLite inputs -> no file-level change signature existed.

Change (phase 2 / owner decision A):
- kanban_annotation_watch.signature: per scope, stat (ino/size/mtime_ns) of every SQLite file the counts and
  narrow key read (hub replica, boards, sync shadows, profile state.db, origin ledger) and their -wal, plus the
  db header change counter and the -shm WAL-index header (moves on every commit even when stat does not), plus
  the scope's mutation cue file. Missing files are part of it; any other error = unknown = moved.
- Holder: after it verifies a scope (narrow key unchanged) it arms a gate (signature, due time, copy read_at).
  While the signature is unchanged and the due time has not come, a pass costs one signature and nothing else:
  no copy load, no narrow key, no lease-side refresh. A watched change, an own kick (now also wakes the loop at
  once via an Event), a foreign mutation cue, an unreadable input, or the due time wakes the full pass.
- Due-time fallback: HOLDER_REFRESH_AGE_S 20 -> 60 s for display-only demand. Exact (strict) callers adopt only
  copies younger than _COUNTS_MAX_AGE_S (30 s) and otherwise read on the poll path (design t01a1d563 C16 /
  review R10), so a strict poll now marks <scope>.strict-demand and the holder keeps the 20 s renewal for
  that scope while it lasts (DEMAND_WINDOW_S).
- Display trust: a holder-verified copy whose recorded watch_sig still equals the current signature stays
  displayable up to DISPLAY_WATCH_MAX_AGE_S (75 s) without header re-stamps; any watched move falls back to the
  unchanged 12 s bound. Poll-published copies carry no watch_sig and keep 12 s. The confirmation re-stamp is
  skipped when nothing watched moved since the last one.
- Strict adoption, exact fingerprints, publication isolation and the 10 s moved floor are unchanged.

Known bound: time-derived narrow-key parts (replica staleness flags, the 180 s observed bucket) and inputs no
watched file reflects are now picked up at the due time (<= 60 s, 20 s under strict demand) instead of <= 12 s.

Tests: new test_kanban_annotation_holder_idle.py (RED on the old holder: 3 refreshes in 50 idle s, 120 narrow
keys per 200 ticks, 20 s fallback; GREEN now), test_kanban_annotation_watch.py (same-stat rollback and WAL
commits move the signature; mutant dropping the counters fails 2/4). Updated floor/narrow/host/regression
pins for the new fallback and strict renewal. 35 annotation/session-activity files: 494 passed, 9 skipped.
